<h1>Live Roller Conveyor Systems</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">A live roller conveyor is any roller conveyor where the rollers are actively driven by a power source, as opposed to <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/gravity/">gravity roller conveyors</a> where rollers spin freely. The three conventional live roller drive technologies are belt-driven live roller (BDLR), line-shaft, and chain-driven live roller (CDLR). <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR (Motor Driven Roller)</a> represents a fourth, newer approach where the motor sits inside the roller itself. This page compares all four technologies head-to-head to help you select the right live roller system for your application.</p>
<h2 id="cdlr-bdlr-heading">Difference Between CDLR and BDLR</h2>
<p>CDLR (chain-driven live roller) drives every roller positively through roller chain and sprockets, while BDLR (belt-driven live roller) drives the rollers by friction from a flat belt running underneath them. Choose CDLR for pallets and heavy loads that must never slip. Choose BDLR for cases, cartons, and totes, especially where the line needs accumulation.</p>
