<h2 id="tech-heading">Four Live Roller Drive Technologies</h2>
<h3>Belt-Driven Live Roller (BDLR)</h3>
<p>BDLR conveyors use a continuous flat belt running beneath the rollers. The belt contacts the underside of each roller through friction. A single AC gearmotor at one end drives the belt via a drive pulley. Tension is maintained by a spring-loaded take-up. BDLR handles the widest load range of the three conventional live roller types, up to 500 lbs per product at speeds of 50-200 FPM.</p>
<p>BDLR provides the foundation for most <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/powered/">powered roller conveyor</a> installations. Hytrol, Dematic, and Intelligrated offer extensive BDLR product lines. With added pneumatic zone controls (belt lifters or pop-up stops), BDLR supports both zero-pressure and minimum-pressure <a href="/conveyor-types/accumulation-conveyors/">accumulation</a>.</p>
<h3>Line-Shaft</h3>
<p>A line-shaft conveyor uses a continuously rotating splined steel shaft running the conveyor length. Individual polyurethane O-ring bands connect each roller to the shaft. The shaft rotates via an AC gearmotor, and O-rings transfer rotation from shaft to roller. Line-shaft conveyors handle up to 300 lbs at 30-180 FPM.</p>
<p>The O-ring connection provides a built-in slip clutch, if a product stops, the O-ring slips on the shaft rather than stalling the motor. This passive slip provides a degree of light <a href="/conveyor-types/accumulation-conveyors/">accumulation</a> without active zone control. Line-shaft works particularly well with pop-up <a href="/conveyor-types/transfer-conveyors/">transfer</a> sections because the O-ring can be disengaged from stopped rollers in the transfer zone without affecting adjacent rollers.</p>
<h3>Chain-Driven Live Roller (CDLR)</h3>
<p><a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR conveyors</a> use roller chains and sprockets to positively drive all rollers. The chain-and-sprocket engagement provides zero-slip positive drive at any load. CDLR handles 500 to over 10,000 lbs per product at 20-120 FPM. CDLR serves as the standard live roller technology for <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">pallet conveyor systems</a> and heavy industrial applications.</p>
<h3>Motor Driven Roller (MDR)</h3>
<p><a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR conveyors</a> place a 24VDC brushless DC motor inside the roller tube itself. Each motor roller drives 2-4 adjacent slave rollers via O-ring bands, creating an independent zone. MDR handles up to 250 lbs per zone at 20-180 FPM. MDR provides built-in zero-pressure accumulation without pneumatics, belts, or chains, and has become the dominant technology for new conveyor installations in distribution and fulfillment.</p>
